<article class="env-lemma" id="06B5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06B5">Lemma <span data-tag="06B5">37.11.8</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a formally smooth morphism of schemes. Then $\Omega _{X/Y}$ is locally projective on $X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose $U \subset X$ and $V \subset Y$ affine open such that $f(U) \subset V$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/02H3" data-tag="02H3">37.11.5</a> $f|_ U : U \to V$ is formally smooth. Hence $\Gamma (V, \mathcal{O}_ V) \to \Gamma (U, \mathcal{O}_ U)$ is a formally smooth ring map, see Lemma <a href="/tag/02H4" data-tag="02H4">37.11.6</a>. Hence by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/031I" data-tag="031I">10.138.7</a> the $\Gamma (U, \mathcal{O}_ U)$-module $\Omega _{\Gamma (U, \mathcal{O}_ U)/\Gamma (V, \mathcal{O}_ V)}$ is projective. Hence $\Omega _{U/V}$ is locally projective, see Properties, Section <a href="/tag/05JN" data-tag="05JN">28.22</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>